     "updated": "2016-12-06T01:13:25.488-0400"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a13a29110000719e8ab1",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": false,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Former user",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a13a29110000719e8ab1",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Sorry, apparently I need to read up more on LDP.  In the Fedora Tech call last week we talked about how the WebAC spec indicates that inheritance should follow containment, but it seems like I was conflating membership and containment.  From what I can tell there isn't a mechanism for specifying a different containment relationship, which I assume might have impacts on functionality.  ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "From what others were saying it would be out of spec for webac to inherit through triples other than the containment, and I'll admit inheriting through arbitrary relations sounds potentially challenging to manage.  So I am not sure how this should proceed.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
